A recursive function, with the two composite nodes as mirror images:

```python
SUCCESS, FAILURE, RUNNING = "SUCCESS", "FAILURE", "RUNNING"

def tick(node, world):
    kind, body = node
    if kind == "cond":
        return SUCCESS if body(world) else FAILURE
    if kind == "act":
        return body(world)
    if kind == "seq":
        for child in body:
            status = tick(child, world)
            if status != SUCCESS:
                return status
        return SUCCESS
    if kind == "fallback":
        for child in body:
            status = tick(child, world)
            if status != FAILURE:
                return status
        return FAILURE
    raise ValueError(f"unknown node kind {kind!r}")
```

An empty sequence succeeds and an empty fallback fails, just as an empty *and* is true and an empty *or* is false. This interpreter is stateless, so it has no halting and no retries; the lesson's class-based version adds both, because real actions keep state (how far the carry has got) that must be reset when they are interrupted.

